f1=finding('RF-001','Adversarial prize semantics can defeat economic delivery while NFT-outcome proceeds are payable','conditional_production_design_violation','High under the explicit untrusted-prize DESIGN scope; trust limitation under the narrower honest-prize interface scope','validated_conditional_path_scope_conflict_open',{'behavior':'high','classification':'medium; explicit scope conflict retained'},[src('DESIGN.md',2,2),src('interfaces/IRaffle.sol',12,15),src('RaffleFactory.sol',127,134,'createRaffle'),src('RaffleFactory.sol',171,177,'_validateCreateParams'),src('Raffle.sol',416,430,'onERC721Received'),src('Raffle.sol',309,337,'redeemWinningTicket'),src('Raffle.sol',375,391,'releaseSponsorProceeds/releaseProtocolFees'),src('Raffle.sol',533,555,'_settleWinningTicket'),src('Raffle.sol',276,294,'enableRefunds')],['Sponsor selects or controls a prize contract that can fabricate ERC165/ownership responses or later reject/seize/pause outgoing transfers.','Victims buy entries sufficient to meet reserve; normal trusted quote token and timely authenticated VRF callback; no quote-token, wrapper or victim-wallet compromise required.'],['Create with a contract that passes the exact configured receipt and reported-ownership checks.','Sell entries, resolve NftWon and permissionlessly settle the valid winning range.','Fabrication variant: token reports winner ownership without honoring the intended ownership/transfer semantics; prize redemption and sponsor release can both appear successful.','Refusal variant: release sponsor proceeds in an earlier transaction, then every NFT redemption reverts. That local rollback cannot recover already paid proceeds; NftWon has no refund transition.'],'Sponsor can retain 95% of gross sales while an entrant has no enforceable promised NFT delivery. Quote liabilities can remain perfectly conserved: this is a cross-asset economic guarantee/trust gap, not demonstrated quote-ledger insolvency. No other raffle is drained.',['Not an exploit against an honest, continuously transferable ERC721 with truthful ownership semantics.','The sealed mock uses a separate actualOwner ledger to illustrate dishonest reports; it is not proof of a particular deployed collection or external market value.','The permanently reverting-prize ordering is source-derived here; no new freeze-token execution campaign was run.'],[proof('runs/DAYBREAK-PASHOV/attempt-01/proofs/UntrustedPrize.t.sol','sealed executable mock source','Lines 73-103 define fake semantics; 142-164 demonstrate creation; 167-192 demonstrate buyer payment, fabricated delivery and 95% sponsor payment.'),proof('runs/DAYBREAK-PASHOV/attempt-01/proofs/untrusted-prize-test.stdout.txt','sealed execution log','Both tests PASS; adjacent exit code is 0; hashes bound by sealed-artifacts.sha256.'),proof('runs/DAYBREAK-SIMAO/attempt-01/FIRST-PASS.md','source review attribution','H-1 through H-4 are explicit function fragments of one chain, not four independent High root causes.')],['Resolve and consistently state whether adversarial prize semantics are actually supported; no owner acceptance or scope relaxation is inferred.','If restricting assets, validate trusted implementations and their upgrade/pause/seizure authority; ERC165 and self-reported ownerOf cannot establish honesty.','Holding both sponsor and treasury proceeds until delivery plus a bounded refund policy can address refusal, but cannot authenticate a lying token; it also changes winner-dependent liveness and requires a complete policy review.'],['Under the chosen supported prize model, entrants cannot lose the retained gross pot without enforceable prize delivery or the specified bounded refund alternative.','Test fabricated receipt/ownerOf, post-escrow pause/seizure, permanent transfer revert, winner refusal, sponsor-before-winner ordering and rollback across separate transactions.','A fix must not claim generic economic authenticity from ownerOf alone.'],['DAYBREAK-SIMAO assigns four High function-level entries; merged here as one economic chain while preserving all IDs.','DAYBREAK-GEBAL rates High; SUP-S1 calls conditional High; SUP-A2 calls conditional Medium; OPENAI-PASHOV/TOB/GEBAL and SUP-A1 retain leads or trust gaps.','Absence of a hostile NFT in production source is not a refutation when adversarial prizes are in DESIGN scope; the sealed mock supplies concrete self-report behavior. Conversely, reviewer agreement does not broaden the honest-prize guarantee.'])
f2=finding('RF-002','Temporal and factory-local destination screening permits sponsor-selected clone sinks','production_configuration_composition','Low','validated_honest_erc721_reproduction',{'behavior':'high','practical_security_relevance':'medium; self-selected recipient loss'},[src('RaffleFactory.sol',105,125,'createRaffle'),src('RaffleFactory.sol',154,178,'_validateCreateParams'),src('Raffle.sol',187,205,'initialize'),src('Raffle.sol',395,405,'releaseSponsorPrize'),src('Raffle.sol',564,566,'_transferQuote'),src('Raffle.sol',593,604,'_isProtocolDestination'),src('Raffle.sol',409,430,'onERC721Received')],['Sponsor deliberately or mistakenly chooses the predictable address of a future clone as immutable sponsorRecipient before it is deployed/registered.','A later successful creation deploys that clone with another configured prize before the first prize release.','Foreign-factory variant additionally needs another deployment and an authorized sponsor/deployer/owner selecting or approving its clone.'],['Create A with sponsorRecipient set to future B; B is code-free and not in the registry.','Create B with token ID 2 and verify B equals the predicted address and is now registered.','Cancel empty A into Refunding and release A token ID 1 through unsafe transferFrom; ownerOf==B passes.','Complete B normally: it releases only configured token ID 2; unrelated token ID 1 stays at B, with no generic execution/rescue route.'],'An honest NFT selected by the sponsor is stranded and the literal no-inter-clone movement promise is violated. A now-known B also makes a sponsor quote release revert and preserve its immutable liability. Foreign-factory quote donations/recipient payouts can become unaccounted holdings; cross-factory ticket-as-prize composition is a scope violation but not necessarily permanent loss.',['No attacker can transform an arbitrary existing victim EOA into a chosen clone.','No theft of another raffle’s quote balance, winner manipulation, or reduction of buyer refund liability is established.','Only the same-factory empty-refund honest-NFT path was executed in recipient-validation; foreign-factory and quote-lock variants remain source-established, separately scoped.'],[proof('reconciliation/recipient-validation/RecipientValidation.t.sol','executable honest ERC721 reproduction','Lines 20-32 predict B, configure A, deploy B, transfer token1 into B, then show B releases only token2.'),proof('runs/TOOL-RECIPIENT-VALIDATION/attempt-01/stdout.txt','execution log','testConfiguredFutureCloneRecipientCanStrandSponsorsOwnPrize PASS; one test; exit 0; integrity checks clean.')],['Repeat current destination screening at sponsor-prize delivery to prevent actual known-clone transfer.','A runtime rejection alone does not make an immutable bad recipient claim recoverable; define supported recipients or separately design authenticated redirection without gifting arbitrary callers destination control.','State whether isolation is same-factory or global; a local registry cannot recognize every foreign deployment or future address.'],['An address accepted before code deployment cannot later receive a sponsor prize if it is then a prohibited protocol destination.','Regression must use honest ERC721, a real future clone, different configured token IDs, and normal completion of the receiving clone; prove claims remain backed on rejection and document any recovery semantics.'],['SUP-A1 calls Informational; SUP-A2 and OPENAI-GEBAL attempt01 call Low; OPENAI-GEBAL attempt02 and DAYBREAK-SIMAO retain self-loss leads.','DAYBREAK-GEBAL and DAYBREAK-TOB emphasize foreign-factory scope. The honest same-factory execution removes that interpretation prerequisite for the temporal variant.'])
f3=finding('OBS-001','Quote issuer sender freeze can block all exits while preserving liabilities','external_dependency_availability','Informational dependency risk; original Medium retained in attribution','conditional_dependency_risk_not_unauthorized_protocol_exploit',{'conditional_control_flow':'high','deployed_exposure':'unverified'},[src('Raffle.sol',349,391,'refundTickets/releases'),src('Raffle.sol',338,342,'redeemWinningTicket'),src('Raffle.sol',564,566,'_transferQuote'),src('interfaces/IRaffle.sol',12,15)],['Configured quote token exercises a sender-wide transfer restriction against the raffle, or otherwise reverts its transfers. No canonical deployment/admin state was supplied.'],['Issuer/dependency blocks raffle sender after deposits.','Every quote transfer reverts; EVM rollback preserves burns, claim balances and other transaction-local state.'],'All quote claimants can be temporarily or indefinitely unable to withdraw; transferability of tickets cannot change the frozen sender.',['No arbitrary participant capability to trigger issuer action demonstrated.','No source-only claim that a deployed USDC instance is currently frozen or that a rescue function can transfer from a blocked sender.'],[],['Document issuer availability and remediation dependencies; an onchain redirect cannot overcome a sender blacklist. Changing quote asset or administrative recovery architecture is a policy change requiring separate review.'],['Injected token transfer refusal must preserve every liability and ticket; restoring transfer capability must restore exits. Distinguish fully backed claims from executable liquidity.'],['DAYBREAK-SIMAO M-1 assigns Medium; supplemental and OpenAI reports treat this as canonical-dependency availability, not a newly demonstrated authorization/accounting flaw.'])
f4=finding('OBS-002','Fixed sponsor or treasury recipient can lose quote-transfer availability','external_dependency_and_recipient_configuration','Informational integration limitation; original Medium retained in attribution','conditional_immutable_recipient_risk',{'conditional_control_flow':'high','deployed_exposure':'unverified'},[src('Raffle.sol',375,391,'releaseSponsorProceeds/releaseProtocolFees'),src('Raffle.sol',564,566,'_transferQuote')],['Issuer freezes a fixed payout recipient after configuration, or that recipient becomes otherwise disallowed.'],['Settlement creates the backed fixed-address claim.','Release fails against the same immutable recipient on every retry; other independently payable recipients can still exit if unaffected.'],'Affected sponsor/treasury claim remains backed but unavailable. This differs from freezing the raffle sender and from theft.',['No current issuer action established; no owner acceptance inferred.','Bearer ticket owners may transfer their ticket if they retain an executable transfer route; fixed proceeds recipients have no equivalent path.'],[],['If recovery is desired, separately design recipient-authorized redirection, authenticate original entitlement and retain sink checks. Account for the stated no-mutable-configuration goal.'],['One blocked fixed recipient must not block sibling claims; authorized recovery must not let an outsider redirect balances.'],['DAYBREAK-SIMAO M-2 assigns Medium; other reports retain an immutable-recipient availability limitation.'])
f5=finding('OBS-003','Nominal quote accounting assumes canonical fee-free non-rebasing transfers','unsupported_quote_semantics','Informational trust assumption','outside_declared_quote_semantics_no_in_scope_exploit',{'conditional_behavior':'high','actual_deployment':'unverified'},[src('RaffleFactory.sol',65,78,'constructor'),src('Raffle.sol',209,236,'buyEntries'),src('Raffle.sol',564,566,'_transferQuote'),src('interfaces/IRaffle.sol',12,15)],['Factory deployer configures an unsupported fee/rebase/false-success token or dependency semantics later depart from the declared canonical behavior.'],['Token returns success while transferring fewer units than nominal purchase or payout.','Ledger records nominal units without balance-delta reconciliation.'],'Unsupported token semantics can underfund liabilities or fake delivery; metadata and six decimals do not prove canonical identity.',['Quote token is explicitly trusted canonical in DESIGN; this is not attacker-selectable per raffle.'],[],['Verify deployed canonical dependency identity and supported semantics; expanding token support requires deliberate accounting design and adversarial-token tests.'],['Supported quote tokens must move exact nominal units; unsupported token tests must be identified as compatibility experiments, not claimed canonical vulnerabilities.'])
f6=finding('OBS-004','Receiver acceptance and address-level ownership do not prove bearer claim usability','recipient_integration_limitation','Informational','self_selected_recipient_limitation',{'behavior':'high'},[src('Raffle.sol',209,236,'buyEntries'),src('Raffle.sol',309,345,'redeemWinningTicket'),src('Raffle.sol',349,371,'refundTickets'),src('Raffle.sol',497,502,'_update')],['Payer/owner/approved operator selects a receiver that accepts the ticket or NFT but cannot later issue the required claim/transfer call; includes inaccessible future or foreign addresses.'],['Safe mint/transfer succeeds or unsafe prize delivery establishes address-level ownership.','Recipient has no usable calling route to exercise the bearer right.'],'Owner-selected claim can be inaccessible despite intact accounting. General last-actor-exit claims require a capable recipient assumption.',['No involuntary loss of a normal EOA established.','A receiver hook acceptance is not a promise of arbitrary future call functionality; runtime sink checks cannot classify every arbitrary contract.'],[],['Document capability requirements; enforce known sink checks; if alternate payout is desired, authenticate current bearer ownership and avoid arbitrary caller routing.'],['Current owner, former owner, operator and incapable receivers must be distinguished; accounting solvency must not be equated with universal claim usability.'])
f7=finding('OBS-005','Unsolicited assets have no rescue and are outside recorded liabilities','intentional_custody_behavior','Informational','documented_design_consequence_not_claim_insolvency',{'source_behavior':'high'},[src('Raffle.sol',409,411,'receiver documentation'),src('Raffle.sol',468,470,'accountedQuoteBalance'),src('Raffle.sol',395,405,'releaseSponsorPrize')],['A sender donates quote tokens, forces native currency, or unsafely transfers an unrelated NFT to the raffle.'],['Asset custody increases without a protocol purchase, allocation or configured prize transition.','No general rescue/execution method exists; only configured claims/prize can exit.'],'Donated assets can be irretrievable. They do not create a liability to the donor, authorize a drain, or make existing claims insolvent under trusted token semantics.',['Do not count raw custody as owed liability. A donation can make actual quote balance exceed accounted liabilities; equality is valid only in a no-donation model.','Counterfactual sponsor-prize delivery in RF-002 is a protocol-directed transfer and is not dismissed as an unsolicited donation.'],[],['Explicitly document no-rescue behavior and scope accounting invariants. A rescue authority would change the immutability/authority model and must not sweep recorded claims.'],['Assert balance >= liabilities under donation scenarios; prove all legitimate claims remain payable and unrelated donations cannot modify settlement or ownership rights.'])
f8=finding('DOC-001','General refund deadline wording omits empty-raffle early cancellation','documentation_alignment','Informational','source_behavior_intended_by_interface_no_buyer_loss',{'behavior':'high'},[src('DESIGN.md',2,2),src('Raffle.sol',279,287,'enableRefunds'),src('interfaces/IRaffle.sol',35,39)],['Sponsor calls while Active and totalEntries==0, or any caller after sale end with no entries.'],['Empty sponsor cancellation can precede sale end; sold raffles must respect their deadline.'],'Design shorthand is less precise than implementation/NatSpec. No paid entrant exists in the early branch.',['Not a premature-refund exploit for a sold raffle.'],[],['Clarify the empty-raffle exception in design text and keep sold/empty paths separate.'],['Before sale end only sponsor may cancel a zero-entry raffle; any positive-entry raffle must reject until its applicable deadline.'])
